# Copy this file to .env (ignored by git) only if you need to override something. Nothing here
# is required: each variable has the default shown, and the defaults are the ones P1 was built
# and measured against.

# Image. The pinned stable one; the model-family image is the fallback when a checkpoint needs
# newer NVFP4 kernels.
# ARL_VLLM_IMAGE=vllm/vllm-openai:v0.27.1

# Weights to load (a Hugging Face id, or a path inside the container). The default is the Qwen3
# 1.7B *chat* model - instruction tuned, unlike the 8B NVFP4 checkpoint that happens to be
# cached on the reference machine.
# ARL_MODEL=Qwen/Qwen3-1.7B

# What clients must ask for. P1 preflights this against /v1/models and refuses to run when the
# two disagree, which is the point: a typo here is a 404 at best and a confusing error at worst.
# ARL_SERVED_NAME=qwen3-1.7b

# ARL_PORT=8000

# A per-request limit, not a memory reservation: enough for single-turn arithmetic by a wide
# margin. Raise it when this server is shared with something that needs long context.
# ARL_MAX_MODEL_LEN=8192

# One request at a time is what this environment is for; more sequences buy queue occupancy that
# P1 cannot use.
# ARL_MAX_NUM_SEQS=8

# Share of the unified 128 GB pool vLLM may CLAIM - a cap, not a consumption. Measured on the
# reference machine: Qwen3-1.7B at 8192 tokens x 8 sequences sat at 3.4 GiB resident under both
# 0.80 and 0.08. 0.08 is the default because a 1.7B model needs roughly 10 GB of headroom at
# most; raise it for a bigger model or a longer context, and do not carry the 27B-era 0.80 over
# by habit. When the pool runs out,
# the failure is earlyoom killing the scheduler.
# ARL_GPU_MEMORY_UTILIZATION=0.08

# Only needed for a gated checkpoint, and: do not commit it. Export it in your shell and add it
# to the service yourself if you need it.
# HF_TOKEN=
